are kept byte-identical to the pinned upstream release and updated by
re-applying upstream's changes, not by editing them here.

What changed
------------
Each change is recorded in docs/fork-plan.md with the measurement or source
reading that motivated it. In summary, with what became of each:

- G1  Codex reasoning records are preserved, minus the opaque ciphertext.
      Merged upstream as #48.
- G2  The Codex event_msg channel is read rather than ignored wholesale.
      The turn-abort half merged as #52. The compaction half is G3.
- G3  Codex compaction records are handled.
      NOT DELIVERED. Codex compaction carries no text summary, and its
      replacement_history is a full message array meaning "replaces the turns
      before this one", so it needs a stateful rewrite plus a default-retention
      policy that was never agreed.
- G4  ~/.codex/archived_sessions/ is discovered. Merged upstream as #45.
- G5  Current-generation DSH session logs (session.vN.jsonl.zstd) are readable.
      Previously 48 of 52 sessions on the test machine were invisible.
      Merged upstream as #44.
- G6  Unknown record types are preserved as ignorable events.
      NOT DELIVERED. DSH honours `ignorable` on read, but its public write path
      (Session.append) threads only sourceEventSeqs and surfaceOp, so an
      external writer cannot set it without hand-encoding the log.
- G7  A recorded working directory can be remapped. Merged upstream as #53.

Two further changes outside that list merged upstream as well: #46 (decoding
`~XXXX` escapes in DSH project directory names) and #51 (splitting the REQ-45
slug assertion into a decode layer and a disk layer).

Added, not derived
------------------
The export half has no upstream counterpart: `packages/codex-archive` reads a
Codex home read-only and writes a portable archive, and
`packages/dsh-session-artifact` is the reference implementation of the DSH
session format used to validate it. The `docs/` tree is this project's own.

Upstream contributions
----------------------
Eleven pull requests were offered upstream, which states in CONTRIBUTING.md
that PRs are welcome for fidelity upgrades. Seven merged: #44, #45, #46, #48,
#51, #52, #53. Four were closed without merging: #47, #49, #50 and #54, because
upstream repaired the same platform failures in f589018 by a route that keeps
Windows path coverage that those four traded away.
